/*
 * Declares the SpecialMathIntOperatorValue class.
 *
 * * SpecialMathIntOperatorValue represents arithmetic operations on integer
 * values that cannot be implemented as a single machine instruction and must
 * instead be delegated to a runtime function. These include operations such as
 * extended‑precision arithmetic, domain‑specific integer transforms, or
 * specialized operators like `^^` that require helper routines.
 *
 * The operator behaves like a binary arithmetic operator but forwards the
 * actual computation to the runtime call stored in `call`. Because the result
 * depends on runtime evaluation, the operator is never considered a full
 * literal.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::operator::binary::int_::special
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/operator/binary/int_/special.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2023-11-10
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
